%I A401092 #10 Oct 16 2026 19:02:50
%S A401092 2,4,21,180,2145,32838,616217,13737608,355734657,10517933610,
%T A401092 350275934745,12993303838188,531852257427569,23831430662754302,
%U A401092 1160887873724369985,61106140628335251984,3457187392704803052801,209247404064885719986770,13492098755211096473876777,923336834846282273557231220
%N A401092 Total number of mutual visibility sets in all labeled trees on n vertices.
%C A401092 A mutual visibilty set in a tree is either the empty set, or the set of vertices of degree at most 1 taken from an induced tree. There is a 1-1 correspondence between these vertices and the induced tree.
%C A401092 a(n) is the total number of induced subgraphs with at most 1 connected component summed over all labeled trees on n vertices. The empty graph induced by an empty set is included here (compare A401091).
%H A401092 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A401092/b401092.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..300</a>
%H A401092 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/VisibilityPolynomial.html">Visibility Polynomial</a>.
%F A401092 a(n) = A401091(n) + A000272(n).
%F A401092 E.g.f.:  B(x) + B(C(x)) where 1 + B(x) is the e.g.f. of A000272 and C(x) is the e.g.f. of A000169.
%o A401092 (PARI) seq(n)={my(u=v=w=O(x)); for(n=1, n, u=x*exp(u); v=x*exp(v+u); w=(w + v)*u); Vec(serlaplace(intformal((u+v+w)/x)))}
%o A401092 (PARI) seq(n) = {my(t=-lambertw(-x + O(x*x^n)), g=-lambertw(-t)); Vec(serlaplace(t - t^2/2 + g - g^2/2))}
%Y A401092 Cf. A000169, A000272, A038058, A401091, A401096.
%K A401092 nonn
%O A401092 1,1
%A A401092 _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 15 2026
